PING in ACK-only packets as quic-go adds it (hysteria client).

quic-go counts the application-data packets it sends that carry only an ACK; once
MaxNonAckElicitingAcks (19) have gone in a row, the next ACK-only packet also carries a PING and
the count starts again, and any packet with other frames resets it (vendor/quic-go/
packet_packer.go:682-708, internal/protocol/params.go:69-71). Initial and Handshake packets never
get that PING.

Upstream ngtcp2 times it instead: a PING once smoothed_rtt has passed since the first of a run of
non-ack-eliciting packets, in the Initial and Handshake spaces as well as 1-RTT, and never in the
ACK-only packets written through ngtcp2_conn_write_single_frame_pkt.

This patch replaces pktns->tx.non_ack_pkt_start_ts with a packet count, drops the rule for the
long-header spaces, and applies the count to ACK-only 1-RTT packets on both write paths.
Applies on top of 0001.

